      "properties": {
        "aux_id": "jackytop/ComfyUI-WanVideoWrapper_jc",
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## SCAIL-2\nhttps://github.com/zai-org/SCAIL-2 — character animation and replacement. The driving video can be the source video itself (end-to-end) or a rendered pose video.\n\n**Models** (`models/diffusion_models`): a single file SCAIL-2 14B checkpoint in Wan key format (the one ComfyUI core loads, or the upstream weights converted with its `convert.py`), bf16 / fp8 / INT8 ConvRot. The loader detects it from `patch_embedding_mask`. Text encoder `umt5-xxl-enc`, CLIP vision `clip_vision_h`, VAE `Wan2_1_VAE`. `rope_function` is switched to `comfy` automatically.\n\n**Settings**\n- 40 steps, cfg 5.0, shift 3, `unipc` (upstream defaults)\n- With the Lightx2v I2V distill LoRA: 8 steps, cfg 1.0, shift 1\n- Width and height divisible by 32; trained at 512p and 704p (e.g. 512x896, 704x1280)\n- Prompt: a long, detailed description of the generated video (character appearance, clothing, background, objects the character interacts with). For replacement, describe the video after the replacement.\n\n**Masks** (they matter): each character gets an identity color, the same one in the reference and the driving mask (blue, red, green, magenta, cyan, yellow). `WanVideo SCAIL2 Colored Mask` turns plain masks (e.g. from SAM2/SAM3) into them; chain one per character through the `prev_*` inputs.\n- Animation Mode: reference mask on white, driving mask on black\n- Replacement Mode (`replacement_mode` on both nodes): reference mask on black, driving mask on white\n\n**References**: extra images in the `ref_image` batch are used as additional references (another view, a close-up, a clean background), each with its mask in the `ref_mask` batch.\n\n**Long videos**: when `num_frames` is larger than `segment_len` (81), the video is generated segment after segment, each starting from the last `segment_overlap` (5) frames of the previous one as clean history, like upstream. Context options also work instead."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
